## 💡 Quick Recap of Completed Work

1. **Core Data Model Schemas**:
   - `parties` & `party_roles` (Vendor, Supplier, Customer, End-Customer, Internal Warehouse)
   - `items` & `item_categories` (20-field Item Enrollment, VMI & Trading Taxonomies, Length/Width/Height cm, Volume cm³, Box CBM, SPQ, SPQ Meter, Buying Price, Selling Price)
   - `locations` (`Rack+Level-Position` e.g. `A1-01`, `location_type`: `receiving_bay`, `inspection`, `storage`, `picking`, `dispatch`, `max_cbm_capacity`)
   - `lots` (Partitioned by `flow_type`: `vmi`, `trading`, `supplies`, Vendor Lot #, FEFO/FIFO dates, PEZA/IP/Invoice refs, USD unit cost)
   - `wrr_documents`, `wrr_items`, and `wrr_inspection_logs` (Pre-receiving email CIPL attachments, Conformance / Non-Conformance tagging, Reason dropdowns, Photo evidence URLs, Vendor Analytics)
   - `forex_rates` (Daily USD-to-PHP exchange rates)
   - `inventory_transactions` (Immutable ledger for receiving, putaway, pick, transfer, reconciliation)

2. **Key Workflows & Business Rules**:
   - **Unified Item Enrollment**: Single form with conditional flow fields saving to one `items` table.
   - **Live `Unit (roll)` $\leftrightarrow$ `Unit (meter)` Synchronization**: Typing in meters auto-fills rolls and vice versa.
   - **Partition Withdrawal SPQ Rules**: VMI & Trading require full SPQ box multiples ($\text{qty} \pmod{\text{spq}} = 0$); Supplies allows piece-level withdrawals ($\text{qty} \ge 1$).
   - **Master Inventory Drill-Down & Received Date**: Item click opens active lot breakdown in FEFO/FIFO order, displaying physical location tags (`A1-01`), Received Date, Pcs/Boxes/CBM, and full transaction history.
   - **Smart Dispersed Putaway & Capacity Preview**: Suggests vacant slots, supports multi-location carton splitting, and displays a location preview card with Flow Type, Item Type, Category, Subcategory, Lot #, and CBM utilization.
   - **Two-Stage Outbound Commitment**: Pick list reserves stock as `committed_qty` (locked against double-picking); physical balance is decremented when floor staff scan barcodes at `dispatch`.
   - **5-Stage Receiving Lifecycle**: CIPL email ingestion $\rightarrow$ Standby database isolation $\rightarrow$ WRR paper print $\rightarrow$ Floor barcode scanning & on-the-fly item enrollment $\rightarrow$ Final receipt confirmation & inventory write.
